{
  "schema": "lr.hunter_activity_poses/1",
  "_about": "Procedural activity poses laid over the humanoid hunter rigs (render/anim/hunter_activity_pose.rs), blended in and out like the player emote poses (data/player/emotes.json). The brain names the activity it is doing (locker_inspect, sniff, look_around, door_push, door_knock, listen, vent_crawl, attack_lunge; corner_peek_left / corner_peek_right come from the corner peek itself); a name with no row here does nothing. A row: blend_in / blend_out (seconds), loop (repeat the keys every `period` seconds; otherwise the last key is held), and keys, each {t, bones: {bone: [x, y, z] degrees}} multiplied onto the clip's pose (a bone a key leaves out is at rest in it). Rotation conventions in this rig (it faces -Z, right is +X): arm X positive raises the arm forward, arm Z positive swings the RIGHT arm out (negative for the left), forearm X positive bends the elbow, chest/belly/pelvis X negative bows forward, head X negative looks down, head Y positive turns to her left, thigh X positive lifts the knee, calf X negative folds the shin back. `peek_clip` is the body clip a peeking hunter plays instead of the walk clip. `scythe` is Kathy's scythe: the hunters that carry it, the clips it swaps in (the replacement must exist in the rig, else the plain clip plays), the one-shot swing clip started when the `swing_on` activity begins, and where the prop model rides (bone, then offset in metres, rotation in degrees, scale). The model must be in the loaded assets (see docs/HUNTER_ANIMATIONS.md). First pass, to tune by eye.",
